<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7162"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 1:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Okay guyses and galses, one thing that has been bugging me lately is the cartooney-type drawing next to the postmarks on the cards.  <BR> <BR>Is the cartoon a post office mark for Wichita? Is it already posted on the postcards from the people who made the cards? Is it a mark from KAKE.TV? Is it BTK&#39;s? What is it? <BR> <BR>Here is one from the Happ Kakeman person: <a href="http://www.geocities.com/for_btk_board/postcardcartoon1.jpg" target=_top>http://www.geocities.com/for_btk_board/postcardcar toon1.jpg</a> <BR> <BR>Here is one from the S Killett person: <a href="http://www.geocities.com/for_btk_board/postcardcartoon2.jpg" target=_top>http://www.geocities.com/for_btk_board/postcardcar toon2.jpg</a> <BR> <BR>Here is a Happ Kakeman postcard which does not show it. It looks like it&#39;s not there, but seems someone has made the picture brighter and you can&#39;t see the cartoon, and you can&#39;t hardly see the post office mark either: <a href="http://www.geocities.com/for_btk_board/postcardcartoon3none.jpg" target=_top>http://www.geocities.com/for_btk_board/postcardcar toon3none.jpg</a> <BR> <BR>---------  <BR> <BR>While we are at it... someone at EZBoard came up with a copy of a picture of the fake employee ID. I don&#39;t know if it&#39;s the real thing, or if that picture was made by the person posting it. It has black ink all over the picture, so I don&#39;t know if BTK did that or if the police did, etc... <BR> <BR>Someone in the other board cleaned the picture and came up with a face: <BR><a href="http://www.geocities.com/for_btk_board/BTKPicture.jpg" target=_top>http://www.geocities.com/for_btk_board/BTKPicture. jpg</a> <BR> <BR>I did one too, but this is the most I could do with it... it shows only the face on the half right side and bottom, this because of the angle the picture was taken and the light on it: <BR><a href="http://www.geocities.com/for_btk_board/postcard5.jpg" target=_top>http://www.geocities.com/for_btk_board/postcard5.j pg</a> . I hope someone can make it out, too. Haha! <BR> <BR>If the police has the fake ID, with a picture on it, then LE should release it because that means that BTK looks similar to the picture and someone may recognize him. Well, I would think. <BR> <BR><IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7162-->
<!--Post: 7167--><!--Time: 1108250327-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7167"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 3:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is a modern artwork of the &#34;Saint Lucy&#34; mentioned in the &#34;BTK confession&#34; in my post#1 <BR> <BR>&#34;Saint Lucy <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.fleckensteingallery.com/lucy.html" target=_top>http://www.fleckensteingallery.com/lucy.html</a> <BR> <BR>that painting make me think of this lines from the &#34;Oh Anna&#34; BTK poem: <BR> <BR>...sun light sparkle tearsin eyes so deep and clear. <BR> <BR>...Alone again I trod in pass memory of mirrors, and ponder why fornumber eight was not. <BR> <BR>Here are som explanation on who &#34;Saint Lucy&#34; is: <BR> <BR><a href="http://64.233.183.104/search?q=cache:60OCsPVPexsJ:en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Lucy%2B%22Saint%2BLucy%2B%22%2B&amp;hl=en" target=_top>http://64.233.183.104/search?q=cache:60OCsPVPexsJ: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Lucy&#43;%22Saint&#43;Lucy&#43;%22 &#43;&amp;hl=en</a> <BR> <BR>and a prayer to &#34;Saint Lucy&#34; the saints for the blind and people with eye problems: <BR><a href="http://64.233.183.104/search?q=cache:KScb-XmKRwwJ:www.catholicsupply.com/existing/lucy.html%2B%22Saint%2BLucy%2B%22%2B&amp;hl=en" target=_top>http://64.233.183.104/search?q=cache:KScb-XmKRwwJ: www.catholicsupply.com/existing/lucy.html&#43;%22Saint &#43;Lucy&#43;%22&#43;&amp;hl=en</a> <BR> <BR>I wish we knew more about what BTK did to the two Otero victims who had bruises around their eyes, did he remove their eyes? <BR> <BR>And did other victims have eye bruises? <BR> <BR>And here are more google images of &#34;Saint Lucy&#34; <BR> <BR><a href="http://images.google.dk/images?q=%22Saint%2BLucy%2B%22%2B&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;safe=off&amp;start=0&amp;sa=N" target=_top>http://images.google.dk/images?q=%22Saint&#43;Lucy&#43;%22 &#43;&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;safe=off&amp;start=0&amp;sa=N</a> <BR> <BR>And to IQ concerning: &#34;The BTK &#34;secret mark&#34; is said to be a pair of&#34; glasses.  <BR> <BR>I read it somwere through my research the last cupple of days, but cant find it now, however &#62;I also found a poster who has been involved in the case due to that she was convinced one of her family members was BTK and have been working with police&#40;her words&#41; and she stated that glasses was NOT the secret mark. So sorry for the confusion. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7167-->
<!--Post: 7225--><!--Time: 1108308560-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7225"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Blade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Blade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 7:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov, <BR>I believe that you are on the mark. Keep it up.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7225-->
<!--Post: 7227--><!--Time: 1108309130-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7227"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 7:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have read that the glasses were used in subliminal message because, in btks drawing of the crime scene, that is the only item he drew sitting on the victims dresser, when there were lots of other items present. The glasses in the sub. mess. may actually be btks artwork. Im not trying to start a rumor here, but it makes sense.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7227-->
<!--Post: 7229--><!--Time: 1108313777-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7229"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 8:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I watch &#34;Dr. G., Criminal Examiner&#34; on the Health Discovery Channel. In one of the episodes a baby is found dead with no apparent sign of foul play, except for very small bruises on his face.  <BR> <BR>Dr. G. then explains that when people are strangled, and too much pressure is applied, blood vessels on the face break and create blotches, which later become bruises. <BR> <BR>So, I&#39;ve been thinking that some of the bruises on the Oteros may have been the product of that, strangulation... except, Mrs. Otero&#39;s cheekbone was said to have been fractured.  <BR> <BR>I guess it would take the person who performed the autopsy to tell us if that is the case, huh? <BR> <BR>p.s. <BR>Did anyone see my post on the cartoon-type character next to the postage stamps on the last two postcards? I want to know what others think of the drawings. Thanks.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7229-->
<!--Post: 7231--><!--Time: 1108314757-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7231"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 9:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It is a cartoon figure of a dog reading the newspaper or looking at something. The object is not shaped like a TV. By a stretch it could be a computer flat screen. From what I understand, the &#39;stamp&#39; for that postcard is printed on the card. Otherwise, I would say look under the stamp. Excellent observation, Ztargate. It might be a worthwhile endeavor for those with subscriptions to look thru the cartoon sections of the paper, unless it is the Post Office&#39;s part of the cancellation process for the stamp.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7231-->
